## Story Description
Review the full Skyscanner mini-app implementation across all src/ files. Checks: TypeScript strict compliance, test coverage (client, CLI, and server each have at least one test file), security (API key never logged or returned in responses, all query params validated), error handling completeness (non-200 upstream responses propagated correctly, missing-param responses return 400), and Express static-file safety (no path traversal). Produce a review document at /tmp/skyscanner-app/review/SKY-006-review.md with findings organised by category. The review passes only when every gating check exits clean.

## Acceptance Criteria
- The file /tmp/skyscanner-app/review/SKY-006-review.md exists and contains all five required sections with exact H2 headings, in order: ## TypeScript, ## Tests, ## Security, ## Error Handling, ## Express Safety
- Running `tsc --noEmit` against the project tsconfig.json (which must set strict: true) exits 0 with no diagnostic output
- Running `vitest run` exits 0; the summary line shows 0 failed, 0 skipped, and 0 todo tests
- At least one non-empty test file targeting each of the three layers is present: a Skyscanner API client test (e.g. src/**/*.client.test.* or equivalent), a CLI entry-point test, and an Express server/route test
- A case-insensitive grep for the literal API key value across all files under src/ and across any captured log/stdout output produces zero matches; no HTTP response body constructed in src/ serialises or forwards the raw key
- Every Express route handler that declares a required query parameter returns HTTP 400 with a non-empty descriptive message string when that parameter is absent, empty, or not a valid value per its documented type
- All code paths that await or call the upstream Skyscanner API wrap the call in try/catch (or equivalent Promise rejection handling) and map non-2xx status codes to a structured JSON error response forwarded to the caller — no unhandled-rejection or uncaught-exception path exists for upstream errors
- Static file serving does not concatenate any user-controlled input directly to __dirname, process.cwd(), or any resolved base path; path.resolve or express.static is used exclusively with a fixed base directory
- The final section of /tmp/skyscanner-app/review/SKY-006-review.md is ## Verdict and contains exactly one of the tokens PASS or FAIL on its own line (greppable as a standalone line); if FAIL, a prioritised numbered list of blocking findings follows immediately under that heading
- The Verdict line is PASS only when all five category checks (TypeScript, Tests, Security, Error Handling, Express Safety) pass; if any single category records a blocking finding the Verdict MUST be FAIL
- The review document is generated by the agent from live inspection of the source files — it must not be a static template; each of the five category sections must reference at least one concrete file path or line-number finding from the actual codebase

